The woman at the desk looks kindly at me.
She asks: "What is your name?"
"My name is Maya," I answer.
She nods and writes my name.
Then she asks: "And how old are you?"
I think for a second.
I smile a little.
"I am thirty-one years old," I say.
She smiles.
"And where do you come from?"
"I come from Mexico," I answer.
She writes it all down on her computer.
My name, my age, and my country.
